# CodeWizard – Jobs Intelligence Webapp (internal tool)
#
# Two data modes are supported. The app auto-detects which one to use:
#
# 1) Supabase mode: if SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY are set AND the
#    `opportunities` table responds, the app reads/writes the Jobs Intelligence
#    tables over the Supabase REST API.
#
# 2) Local files mode (fallback): if the vars are missing, or Supabase is not
#    reachable / the tables do not exist, the app reads JSON files from
#    /Users/nirg/repositories/CodeWizard/Jobs/data/:
#       opportunities.json, signals.json, companies.json, people.json, scans.json
#    Each file may be a JSON array or { "items": [ ... ] }.
#    Missing files are treated as empty. Updates are in-memory only.
#
# If the vars are not present in the environment, the app also tries to read
# them from /Users/nirg/repositories/CodeWizard/web/.env at import time.

SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your-publishable-anon-key
